\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[calc(185px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] lg:scroll-mt-[calc(126px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] mb-10 last:mb-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-1.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-book-open h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1akyts\",{\"d\":\"M12 7v14\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"ruj8y\",{\"d\":\"M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base font-medium\",\"children\":\"Documentation\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],null]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Guides, cookbooks, and tools for building with TypeSafe: Jev 1.13 on OpenRouter.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border border-none p-0\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L7a\",null,{\"resources\":[{\"type\":\"guide\",\"title\":\"Jev Tutorial\",\"href\":\"/docs/guides/community/jev-tutorial\"},{\"type\":\"guide\",\"title\":\"Jev (TypeSafe)\",\"href\":\"/docs/guides/community/jev\"},{\"type\":\"guide\",\"title\":\"TypeSafe SDK (Jev)\",\"href\":\"/docs/guides/community/typesafe-sdk\"},{\"type\":\"cookbook\",\"title\":\"Gate Agent Tool Calls with Jev\",\"href\":\"/docs/cookbook/building-agents/gate-tool-calls-with-jev\"},{\"type\":\"cookbook\",\"title\":\"Auto-Approve Coding Agent Permission Prompts with Jev\",\"href\":\"/docs/cookbook/coding-agents/auto-approve-permission-prompts-with-jev\"},{\"type\":\"cookbook\",\"title\":\"Classify Reddit and YouTube Comments with Jev and ScrapeCreators\",\"href\":\"/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/classify-reddit-comments-with-jev\"},{\"type\":\"cookbook\",\"title\":\"Classify and Tag Text at Scale with Jev\",\"href\":\"/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/jev-classification\"},{\"type\":\"cookbook\",\"title\":\"Cut LLM Cost with a Jev-Verified Cascade\",\"href\":\"/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/jev-verified-cascade\"},{\"type\":\"lab\",\"title\":\"Jev Lab\",\"href\":\"/labs/jev\"}],\"page\":\"model\"}]}]]}]\n7c:T422,The Jev 1.13 documentation on OpenRouter includes the [Jev Tutorial](/docs/guides/community/jev-tutorial) guide, the [Jev (TypeSafe)](/docs/guides/community/jev) guide, the [TypeSafe SDK (Jev)](/docs/guides/community/typesafe-sdk) guide, the [Gate Agent Tool Calls with Jev](/docs/cookbook/building-agents/gate-tool-calls-with-jev) cookbook, the [Auto-Approve Coding Agent Permission Prompts with Jev](/docs/cookbook/coding-agents/auto-approve-permission-prompts-with-jev) cookbook, the [Classify Reddit and YouTube Comments with Jev and ScrapeCreators](/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/classify-reddit-comments-with-jev) cookbook, the [Classify and Tag Text at Scale with Jev](/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/jev-classification) cookbook, the [Cut LLM Cost with a Jev-Verified Cascade](/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/jev-verified-cascade) cookbook, and the interactive [Jev Lab](/labs/jev). The [quickstart](/docs/quickstart) covers API keys and your first request, and the [API reference](/docs/api-reference/overview) lists every parameter.7d:T742,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is Jev 1.13?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Jev is a structured decision model from TypeSafe, and the first of its System One models. System One models make fast, structured decisions for software, returning a typed choice rather than free-form text. It is suited for routing, classification, and other decision points inside an application where a fast, predictable answer matters more than generated prose.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Where is the Jev 1.13 documentation?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The Jev 1.13 documentation on OpenRouter includes the Jev Tutorial guide, the Jev (TypeSafe) guide, the TypeSafe SDK (Jev) guide, the Gate Agent Tool Calls with Jev cookbook, the Auto-Approve Coding Agent Permission Prompts with Jev cookbook, the Classify Reddit and YouTube Comments with Jev and ScrapeCreators cookbook, the Classify and Tag Text at Scale with Jev cookbook, the Cut LLM Cost with a Jev-Verified Cascade cookbook, and the interactive Jev Lab. The quickstart covers API keys and your first request, and the API reference lists every parameter.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How much does Jev 1.13 cost?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Jev 1.13 costs $0.042/M input tokens and $0.00/M output tokens.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the context length of Jev 1.13?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Jev 1.13 has a 32,000 token context window.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What inputs and outputs does Jev 1.13 support?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Jev 1.13 accepts text as input and returns structured decisions.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"When was Jev 1.13 released?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Jev 1.13 was released on September 18, 2026.\"}}]}76:[[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"id\":\"faq\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[calc(185px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] lg:scroll-mt-[calc(126px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] mb-10 last:mb-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-circle-question-mark h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"circle\",\"1mglay\",{\"cx\":\"12\",\"cy\":\"12\",\"r\":\"10\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1u773s\",{\"d\":\"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"p32p05\",{\"d\":\"M12 17h.01\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base font-medium\",\"children\":\"Frequently asked questions\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],null]}],null,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border border-none p-0\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L7b\",null,{\"faqs\":[{\"question\":\"What is Jev 1.13?\",\"answer\":\"Jev is a structured decision model from TypeSafe, and the first of its System One models. System One models make fast, structured decisions for software, returning a typed choice rather than free-form text. It is suited for routing, classification, and other decision points inside an application where a fast, predictable answer matters more than generated prose.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"Where is the Jev 1.13 documentation?\",\"answer\":\"$7c\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"How much does Jev 1.13 cost?\",\"answer\":\"Jev 1.13 costs $0.042/M input tokens and $0.00/M output tokens.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"What is the context length of Jev 1.13?\",\"answer\":\"Jev 1.13 has a 32,000 token context window.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"What inputs and outputs does Jev 1.13 support?\",\"answer\":\"Jev 1.13 accepts text as input and returns structured decisions.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"When was Jev 1.13 released?\",\"answer\":\"Jev